From 93dc6f80f821cebc1f0f68c5b028877d53d05c26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:47:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] hw/arm/mt7981: Airoha AN8855 switch, 512 MiB SPI-NAND
 (Routerich BE7200)

gmac0=an8855: the Airoha AN8855 5-port gigabit switch at MDIO address 1,
as on the Routerich BE7200 (MT7987A).  Page 4 of its MDIO address is the
32-bit register bus (PBUS: 0x11/0x12 write address, 0x13/0x14 write
data, 0x15/0x16 read address, 0x17/0x18 read data); the other pages and
addresses 1..5 reach the internal PHYs (ID c0ff:0410).  Its registers are
translated into the MT7531 model the forwarding uses (CPU port 5 instead
of 6, PCR / port matrix / PVC / PVID, VLAN table via VTCR/VAWD0/VARD0,
address table commands, PMSR link status, CREV 0x8855, HWTRAP, soft
reset), so the MTK special tag, VLANs and learning work as on the MT7531.
OpenWrt's U-Boot ("Net: Airoha AN8855") and Linux (an8855 DSA driver,
air_an8855 PHYs) bring the LAN ports up.

nand=512: Winbond W25N04KV (ID ef aa 23), 4096 blocks, 2048 + 128 byte
pages, two planes (the plane select bit of the column address is
ignored).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
